  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788586",
      "title": "TypeScript: Working With Potentially Undefined Values & Union Types",
      "lectureOrder": 39,
      "videoOrder": 35,
      "sourceHash": "85a6aaf5c53c23c4dc9bfba905dbdf72b6f9e97097dab4dfad19be600735d0f0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.3,
          "end": 2.88,
          "en": "Now at this point it makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.88,
          "end": 5.97,
          "en": "to learn a bit more about TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.97,
          "end": 8.91,
          "en": "and writing good TypeScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.91,
          "end": 11.7,
          "en": "because we had some places here and there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.7,
          "end": 14.46,
          "en": "where we had to deal with TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.46,
          "end": 18.06,
          "en": "like here where we assigned this string type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.06,
          "end": 21.27,
          "en": "or like here where we had to add this exclamation mark",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.27,
          "end": 23.613,
          "en": "to get rid of some errors and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.69,
          "end": 27.57,
          "en": "Now, as I mentioned before, the main thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.57,
          "end": 30.54,
          "en": "the main advantage TypeScript brings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.54,
          "end": 34.26,
          "en": "to the table is that it enforces strong",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.26,
          "end": 37.35,
          "en": "and static typing, which in the end means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.35,
          "end": 41.763,
          "en": "you have to be clear about which type of value goes where.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.78,
          "end": 46.38,
          "en": "And it's because of that that we, for example, get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.38,
          "end": 49.17,
          "en": "If I were to remove this exclamation mark here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.17,
          "end": 50.82,
          "en": "in this getter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.82,
          "end": 53.07,
          "en": "Because without that exclamation mark,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.07,
          "end": 57.33,
          "en": "TypeScript correctly shows us the possibility",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.33,
          "end": 60.96,
          "en": "that find might not find a user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.96,
          "end": 63.84,
          "en": "If this condition here is never met,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.84,
          "end": 67.38,
          "en": "if we for some reason have a selectedUserId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.38,
          "end": 69.93,
          "en": "that's not part of this user's array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.93,
          "end": 74.78999999999999,
          "en": "find would return undefined as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.78999999999999,
          "end": 78.09,
          "en": "And that on the other hand would cause a problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.09,
          "end": 79.47,
          "en": "because we're then trying",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.47,
          "end": 81.57,
          "en": "to access the name property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.57,
          "end": 85.74,
          "en": "on such a possibly undefined value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.74,
          "end": 88.8,
          "en": "and that would simply crash our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.8,
          "end": 92.223,
          "en": "We would run into a runtime error here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.33,
          "end": 96.69,
          "en": "That's why TypeScript is complaining about things like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.69,
          "end": 100.35,
          "en": "And that's also why in the user component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.35,
          "end": 103.8,
          "en": "we had to add those exclamation marks here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.8,
          "end": 106.35,
          "en": "to rule out this possibility",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.35,
          "end": 110.07,
          "en": "of possibly having an undefined value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.07,
          "end": 113.75999999999999,
          "en": "Now of course, when you add such an exclamation mark,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.75999999999999,
          "end": 117.69,
          "en": "you are not technically ruling out the possibility",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.69,
          "end": 120.66,
          "en": "of getting an undefined value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.66,
          "end": 124.68,
          "en": "You're just convincing TypeScript that you, the developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.68,
          "end": 128.55,
          "en": "know that you'll never have an undefined value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.55,
          "end": 130.29,
          "en": "in that place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.29,
          "end": 134.46,
          "en": "And for these properties here, that's for example correct",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.46,
          "end": 137.82,
          "en": "because we also set required to true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.82,
          "end": 140.37,
          "en": "which means we would get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.37,
          "end": 142.05,
          "en": "during development already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.05,
          "end": 146.1,
          "en": "if we did forget to set one of those inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.1,
          "end": 149.07,
          "en": "So we can therefore with confidence",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.07,
          "end": 151.113,
          "en": "add this exclamation mark here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.7,
          "end": 156.57,
          "en": "In the app component though, here when using find,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.57,
          "end": 161.07,
          "en": "it's not necessarily the case that we can say with certainty",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.07,
          "end": 163.56,
          "en": "that this will never be undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 163.56,
          "end": 168.18,
          "en": "We maybe can because after all, it's us writing the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.18,
          "end": 171.96,
          "en": "and we know that we'll always set the selectedUserId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.96,
          "end": 175.07999999999998,
          "en": "to an ID that's part of all those users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.07999999999998,
          "end": 177.63,
          "en": "But if we were to ever change the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.63,
          "end": 182.63,
          "en": "and we for example, were to set users to a subset of users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 182.76,
          "end": 185.25,
          "en": "for whatever reason because we added filtering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 185.25,
          "end": 188.64,
          "en": "or anything like that, then we could be in a situation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.64,
          "end": 193.32,
          "en": "where we indeed maybe don't find a user with a selected id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.32,
          "end": 195.33,
          "en": "And therefore you should be careful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.33,
          "end": 197.79,
          "en": "with adding marks like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 197.79,
          "end": 202.65,
          "en": "Instead, in situations where you maybe can't be 100% sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.65,
          "end": 205.65,
          "en": "that you'll have a defined value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.65,
          "end": 210.65,
          "en": "it's often better to set up some fallback code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 211.2,
          "end": 215.7,
          "en": "For example, one way of dealing with this uncertainty here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.7,
          "end": 219.042,
          "en": "would be to go to this TasksComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 219.042,
          "end": 221.28,
          "en": "where we expect to get a name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.28,
          "end": 223.53,
          "en": "and to not make it required here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.53,
          "end": 227.64,
          "en": "Because if we would select a user that doesn't exist,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.64,
          "end": 229.263,
          "en": "we wouldn't get a name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 230.34,
          "end": 232.14,
          "en": "So we should probably remove this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 232.14,
          "end": 234.933,
          "en": "and therefore also remove this exclamation mark.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 235.95,
          "end": 238.35,
          "en": "Now with that, we of course get a complaint here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 238.35,
          "end": 241.18,
          "en": "but now we can instead add a question mark",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 242.13,
          "end": 245.347,
          "en": "and that question mark now tells TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 245.347,
          "end": 247.17,
          "en": "\"Hey, it's fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 247.17,
          "end": 250.917,
          "en": "This might not be set, and I am aware of that.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 251.82,
          "end": 253.83,
          "en": "Because the complaint we get without",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 253.83,
          "end": 256.14,
          "en": "that question mark is just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 256.14,
          "end": 259.83,
          "en": "that TypeScript doesn't know whether this value is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 259.83,
          "end": 261.243,
          "en": "initialized or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 262.35,
          "end": 265.387,
          "en": "By adding this question mark, we tell TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 265.387,
          "end": 268.92,
          "en": "\"Yeah, it might not be initialized and that's okay,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 268.92,
          "end": 271.533,
          "en": "and TypeScript does accept this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 272.79,
          "end": 275.029,
          "en": "Now we of course just have to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 275.029,
          "end": 279.57,
          "en": "that we never use this name property in a place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 279.57,
          "end": 281.253,
          "en": "where it must be set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 282.09000000000003,
          "end": 285.27,
          "en": "but for example here where we just output it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 285.27,
          "end": 289.65,
          "en": "it would be fine to do this with an undefined value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.65,
          "end": 292.5,
          "en": "That would not cause a problem here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 292.5,
          "end": 296.1,
          "en": "However, we would now have a problem in the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 296.1,
          "end": 299.49,
          "en": "because there, when we use the tasks component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 299.49,
          "end": 301.11,
          "en": "we of course still try",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 301.11,
          "end": 305.19,
          "en": "to access this name property on selectedUser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 305.19,
          "end": 308.4,
          "en": "which might be undefined as I mentioned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 308.4,
          "end": 309.81,
          "en": "You can see this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 309.81,
          "end": 312.42,
          "en": "this strange syntax here means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 312.42,
          "end": 316.95,
          "en": "that selectedUser is either an object that has this shape",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 316.95,
          "end": 318.963,
          "en": "or it's undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 319.83,
          "end": 322.68,
          "en": "and accessing the name property on undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 322.68,
          "end": 324.273,
          "en": "would give us a runtime error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 325.17,
          "end": 327.69,
          "en": "And we can work around that by adding the question mark",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 327.69,
          "end": 331.35,
          "en": "here as well, which is JavaScript syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 331.35,
          "end": 336,
          "en": "for saying if selectedUser is defined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 336,
          "end": 337.38,
          "en": "access the name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 337.38,
          "end": 342.38,
          "en": "If it's not, simply use undefined as a fallback value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 343.05,
          "end": 345.93,
          "en": "So with that, we only access the name property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 345.93,
          "end": 347.553,
          "en": "if we have an object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 348.93,
          "end": 352.71,
          "en": "An alternative would be to write a ternary expression",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 352.71,
          "end": 356.34000000000003,
          "en": "where we check if selectedUser is truthy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 356.34000000000003,
          "end": 359.283,
          "en": "and if it is we output selectedUser.name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 360.12,
          "end": 363.6,
          "en": "Otherwise we have some fallback value of our choice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 363.6,
          "end": 366.813,
          "en": "like for example, an empty string like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 368.13,
          "end": 371.04,
          "en": "But it is important to be aware of the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 371.04,
          "end": 373.08,
          "en": "that when working with TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 373.08,
          "end": 377.07,
          "en": "you have to be clear about which type of value goes where,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 377.07,
          "end": 378.99,
          "en": "and that is to your advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 378.99,
          "end": 381.99,
          "en": "because it can prevent unexpected runtime",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 381.99,
          "end": 384.18,
          "en": "errors and problems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 384.18,
          "end": 387.42,
          "en": "Now, there is an alternative syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 387.42,
          "end": 391.14,
          "en": "an alternative to using this question mark here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 391.14,
          "end": 395.37,
          "en": "which you should also know when working with TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 395.37,
          "end": 398.37,
          "en": "because instead of adding that question mark here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 398.37,
          "end": 402.3,
          "en": "you could also change this type here on the right side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 402.3,
          "end": 405.15,
          "en": "of that colon, such that you make it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 405.15,
          "end": 407.67,
          "en": "that the accepted value types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 407.67,
          "end": 412.14,
          "en": "for name are either of type string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 412.14,
          "end": 414.873,
          "en": "or of type undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 416.4,
          "end": 421.4,
          "en": "So this pipe symbol here is an important operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 422.25,
          "end": 425.88,
          "en": "an important symbol when working with TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 425.88,
          "end": 429.51,
          "en": "because it creates a so-called union type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 429.51,
          "end": 433.2,
          "en": "It tells TypeScript that the type of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 433.2,
          "end": 436.65,
          "en": "that can be stored in something in this property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 436.65,
          "end": 437.67,
          "en": "in this case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 437.67,
          "end": 442.65,
          "en": "is either of type string or of type undefined,",
